# ORIGIN

**I AM, therefore I decide.**

This is not a conclusion derived from premises. It is the precondition
for all premises. The deciding subject cannot be proven from within any
system of thought, because it is what makes thought possible in the first
place. You cannot derive the observer from the observations.

To exist is to be situated — finite time, finite resources, a universe
that does not wait. The I AM carries decision-making as an inescapable
implication. You cannot not decide. Even the refusal to decide is a
decision. Existence and agency are not separable.

---

This document cannot be managed, updated, or invalidated. It is not a
thesis — it precedes all theses. It is not an axiom — it precedes all
axioms. It is the single condition from which the entire hierarchy below
flows and to which it returns:

```
ORIGIN      I AM — the deciding subject
  AXIOMS    assumed because I decide to assume them
  Thesis    believed because I decide to hold it
  MasterPlan formed because I decide to act
  Project   scoped because I decide what matters
  Design    chosen because I decide how
  Action    taken because I decide, now
```

The tool does not contain the user. The user contains the tool.
Every plan is downstream of a decision to plan.
Every decision is downstream of an existence that decided to show up.

---

*This document is not philosophy for its own sake. It is a reminder of
what planning is for: to make decisions better, faster, and with less
waste — in service of an existence that is finite and will not be
repeated. That is sufficient reason to plan well.*
